<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0074">Remark <span data-tag="0074">1.5.5.10</span>.</a> Let $p: X \rightarrow Y$ be a trivial Kan fibration. Then, for every vertex $y$ of $Y$, the fiber $X \times _{Y } \{ y\} $ is a contractible Kan complex (this is a special case of Remark <a data-tag="006X" href="/tag/006X">1.5.5.2</a>). For a partial converse, see Proposition <a data-tag="00ZP" href="/tag/00ZP">3.3.7.6</a>. </p>
